1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,880
- You ditched work
to listen to Dr. Pun again

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:03,640
- You can’t keep living like this.

3
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:05,200
- Are you still playing Cupid?

4
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:06,000
- Hello.

5
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,240
- Are you Mr. Monsieur?

6
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:08,240
- You’re here for the blind date, too?

7
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:10,720
- I’ll show you how many matches I get.

8
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:13,120
- Are you sure you don’t want to rank anyone?

9
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:14,560
- What are you doing, Dean?

10
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:15,680
- Are you trying to match with everyone?

11
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:18,040
- I believe in equality.

12
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:21,960
- [SURFING DOLPHIN]

13
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:27,080
- [SURFING DOLPHIN,
NUMBER OF MATCHES: 1]

14
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:52,320
[SPICY PORK BACKBONE SOUP]

15
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:16,920
So we just put these on and dig in?

16
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:30,280
Whoa. They’re huge.

17
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:33,960
You said there were bones and chilies.

18
00:02:35,079 --> 00:02:35,960
Why do you want to eat this?

19
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:38,560
Well, I want to try it.

20
00:02:39,320 --> 00:02:40,200
Ever heard of ‘being open-minded’?

21
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:46,040
What’s wrong with you?

22
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:47,640
When I disagree with you, you get mad.

23
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,680
When I spoil you, you pick a fight.

24
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:05,320
Hmm, it’s pretty good.

25
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:09,280
Are you trying to comfort me?

26
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:13,120
No, it’s actually good.

27
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:32,240
Okay.

28
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:35,480
Do I like it? No.

29
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:40,440
But now that I’ve tried it, I get why you like it.

30
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:49,200
Here, eat.

31
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:19,480
Hot and spicy as always.

32
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:23,400
Feeling better now?

33
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:26,840
Why?

34
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:30,200
Is it so obvious that I’m in a terrible mood?

35
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:32,120
No.

36
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:38,840
But they say eating something you like
makes you feel better.

37
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:42,520
So you’re spoiling me
because you think I’m upset?

38
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:44,800
That’s why you brought me here, right?

39
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:48,159
What else could I do?

40
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:50,040
We matched, so I have to stick with you.

41
00:04:51,159 --> 00:04:51,840
Those are the rules.

42
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:54,760
I couldn’t stand
spending time with someone moody,

43
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:56,760
I couldn’t stand
spending time with someone moody,

44
00:04:57,760 --> 00:04:58,240
No way.

45
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:12,160
Thank you…

46
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:16,480
for taking pity on me.

47
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:23,360
What’s there to pity?

48
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:26,520
You just didn’t get matched with anyone else

49
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:28,800
but me.

50
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:31,920
That.

51
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:34,560
Thank you.

52
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:41,880
Eat up. Isn’t this your favorite?

53
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:15,200
I forgot.

54
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:17,240
(Oh, come on!)

55
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:18,760
(That’s your excuse?)

56
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:20,320
(You’ve been getting
smoother every day, jackass.)

57
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:21,640
Sorry.

58
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:22,840
I’m sorry, Jo.

59
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:24,960
You’ve never been like this, dude.

60
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:27,040
I opened a new club,

61
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:28,960
(and you haven’t come by even once.)

62
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:30,400
(Jo said it himself.)

63
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:32,000
(You gotta come.)

64
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:33,920
I have plans with Moth.

65
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:36,080
(There it is. My guess is never wrong.)

66
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:38,320
(Being with your special someone is fine,)

67
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:40,440
(but you gotta make time
for your friends too, man.)

68
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:42,480
Hey, I gotta go.

69
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:58,159
Did I keep you waiting?

70
00:06:59,159 --> 00:06:59,760
Yeah.

71
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:01,200
Sorry.

72
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:02,440
Come on in.

73
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:14,800
What were you doing?

74
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:17,240
What took you so long?

75
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:18,880
I was on the phone.

76
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:22,800
Ohm and Boom asked if
I wanted to go to Jo’s new club.

77
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:24,400
I knew it.

78
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:26,560
It’s Friday night.

79
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:28,240
Aren’t you going out?

80
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:29,480
No.

81
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:32,200
I want to stay in with you.

82
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:34,800
Ouch.

83
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:38,200
Ouch, that hurts.

84
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:39,080
So dramatic.

85
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:41,400
I meant I want to get inside the house.

86
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:42,760
What are you thinking?

87
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:44,640
I’m not having dirty thoughts like you..

88
00:07:48,840 --> 00:07:49,360
[5 G-CH 203, BANGKOK]

89
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:52,480
Do you usually drive?

90
00:07:53,400 --> 00:07:54,240
I’ve never seen you drive.

91
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:58,240
Bangkok traffic is horrible.
I get frustrated on the road.

92
00:07:58,720 --> 00:07:59,159
Why?

93
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:02,320
Wanna be my passenger princess?

94
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:04,600
What kind of joke is that?

95
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:05,880
Lame.

96
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:26,480
Do you really live alone?

97
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:28,840
Why?

98
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:32,880
It looks like you live with your mom.

99
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:35,400
I do live alone.

100
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:37,240
My older sister comes to visit
from time to time.

101
00:08:37,640 --> 00:08:39,200
My parents barely ever come by.

102
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:42,080
Why?

103
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:44,360
Is it hard to believe?

104
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:46,760
Well?

105
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:48,320
What are you cooking for me?

106
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:56,120
What do you feel like eating?

107
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:08,840
Hey.

108
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:12,000
You asked me over for food.

109
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:13,040
So let’s eat food.

110
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:25,720
Did you steal a restaurant’s fridge?

111
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:28,280
What?

112
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:31,520
Come on. What an exaggeration.

113
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:38,640
Hey, we’ve got some chuck.

114
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:40,800
How about steak?

115
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:42,320
Mm.

116
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,640
What’s this?

117
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Snakeskin gourami?

118
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,400
Yeah. Why?

119
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:52,640
Want some?

120
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,560
Straight from a premium farm.

121
00:09:58,280 --> 00:10:00,240
What are these?

122
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:01,880
Stocks.

123
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,880
Kombu stock and chicken stock.

124
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:05,280
I make them whenever I have time.

125
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:06,600
Saves time when I wanna cook.

126
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:10,800
Who the heck are you?

127
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:13,360
All set.

128
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:22,520
Need some help?

129
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:25,720
Make a salad.

130
00:10:27,280 --> 00:10:27,760
Sure.

131
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:55,480
Oh, there’s some cos lettuce in the fridge.

132
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:56,560
You can add that too.

133
00:10:58,360 --> 00:10:59,520
What’s cos lettuce?

134
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:01,080
Are you serious?

135
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:04,560
Hold this for a sec.

136
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:11,200
This is cos lettuce.

137
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:14,760
I thought it was called salad veggie.

138
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:20,400
If you’re gonna call it that, just call it lettuce.

139
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:22,360
Ouch.

140
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:25,240
It’s splattering!

141
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:28,520
Hold on.

142
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:32,360
Here.

143
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:00,960
Abracadabra! All better now.

144
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:13,400
Go have a seat.

145
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:16,760
Chef Dean will take care of everything.

146
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:10,200
Have a bite.

147
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:24,240
How is it? Good?

148
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:29,240
Pretty good.

149
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:32,520
Pretty good? Meaning?

150
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:36,800
Pretty good means delicious.

151
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:45,400
Will you stay over tonight?

152
00:13:49,280 --> 00:13:50,280
Let me think about it.

153
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:14,160
You did a big cleanup to welcome me?

154
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:15,880
It always looks like this.

155
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:27,560
Can I have that back?

156
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:28,960
Forgot to put it away.

157
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:45,840
How many people have been in this room?

158
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:48,280
Have you ever counted?

159
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:49,960
I’ve never brought anyone here.

160
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:53,320
Hey, I’m serious.

161
00:14:57,360 --> 00:15:00,080
So I’m the first?

162
00:15:04,160 --> 00:15:04,760
Mm.

163
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:12,080
I may babble a lot,
but I’m telling the truth this time.

164
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:14,880
I’m not lying.

165
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:20,720
You’re the first person
I’ve ever brought into my room.

166
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:39,640
I can swear to it if you want.

167
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:52,280
I never said I didn’t believe you.

168
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:31,960
Is the tee comfy enough?

169
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:34,520
Yeah, it is.

170
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,680
If it’s too tight, I’ll get you a new one.

171
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:44,160
Why does it say ‘Love’ here, not ‘Live’?

172
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:46,800
They printed it wrong.

173
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:51,240
So it’s more special than the others.

174
00:16:59,120 --> 00:17:02,080
Sit back and relax.
Let me take care of you.

175
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:46,600
Hey.

176
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:51,720
Dean.

177
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:04,360
I can’t sleep.

178
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:08,200
Is it too cold?

179
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:16,320
Or… is the mattress too soft?

180
00:18:18,520 --> 00:18:18,880
No.

181
00:18:21,920 --> 00:18:22,840
I’m just not used to it.

182
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:25,440
I’m more comfortable in my own room.

183
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:29,120
Can I go home?

184
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:33,600
Okay.

185
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:35,320
I’ll book you a ride.

186
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:41,880
It’s okay. I can do it.

187
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:11,160
[I’M HOME.]

188
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:20,160
[SWEET DREAMS.]

189
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:30,560
[I’M SORRY.]

190
00:19:37,120 --> 00:19:39,720
[IT’S ALL GOOD.
WASH THE TEE, THOUGH.]

191
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:19,120
Yeah?

192
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:20,240
(Morning.)

193
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:21,280
Going anywhere today?

194
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:22,120
Staying in.

195
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:23,160
Got some work to do.

196
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:25,360
Where will you go after that?

197
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:27,520
I’ve got a Zoom meeting with a new client.

198
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:29,280
I don’t know when we’ll wrap up—

199
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:30,160
Hi, Moth.

200
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:32,280
Can we borrow Dean
for a sec for some content?

201
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:34,560
Hey, are you guys working?

202
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,280
(Then get to work.)

203
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:38,000
I’m hanging up.

204
00:20:45,480 --> 00:20:45,800
Hey.

205
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:47,640
Why the hell did you two
have to show up now?

206
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:51,080
It’s been so hard to see you lately.

207
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:52,000
You’re so clingy to your boyfriend.

208
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,120
Moth and I aren’t boyfriends.

209
00:20:53,280 --> 00:20:54,520
Oh, really?

210
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:57,880
But you two are acting
more like a couple than we do.

211
00:20:58,400 --> 00:20:58,800
Oops.

212
00:21:00,120 --> 00:21:02,240
But our couple is still the best.

213
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:04,560
Aww, are you sulking?

214
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:07,080
There, there.

215
00:21:07,080 --> 00:21:07,920
There.

216
00:21:10,040 --> 00:21:11,640
(I just saw your status, Mr. Bagel.)

217
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:13,480
(Any updates for us?)

218
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:15,480
It’s nothing.

219
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:17,600
I just posted it for good luck.

220
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:20,720
And I’m just hoping
something good comes my way.

221
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:23,600
(Is it about the blind date thing you went to?)

222
00:21:24,040 --> 00:21:25,080
(Do we have some good news?)

223
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:28,480
If you mean him, then no.
We’re not talking anymore.

224
00:21:29,720 --> 00:21:32,800
Actually, you can ask Mr. Monsieur too.

225
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:35,080
He also went to the blind date event.

226
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:40,800
I…

227
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:44,600
I didn’t see or talk to anyone.

228
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:47,880
I… had to rush home.

229
00:21:47,880 --> 00:21:49,280
(What a shame.)

230
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:52,040
(I thought Mr. Bagel
and Mr. Monsieur might get to meet.)

231
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:57,640
Anyway, is everyone
coming to the Good Boi Party?

232
00:21:57,800 --> 00:21:59,320
You guys aren’t bailing on me, are you?

233
00:21:59,320 --> 00:22:00,800
(Of course we’re coming.)

234
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:04,480
(I’m about to prepare
crispy chicken for everyone’s pup.)

235
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:07,000
Come, come.

236
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:09,640
I want to meet you all.

237
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:14,760
It sounds fun.

238
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:17,600
Right?

239
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:21,840
You’re not gonna back out on me,
are you, Mr. Monsieur?

240
00:22:23,440 --> 00:22:26,760
If we don’t get to meet,
I’m seriously going to be mad at you.

241
00:22:34,520 --> 00:22:35,800
What should Daddy do, baby girl?

242
00:22:53,360 --> 00:22:53,680
Here.

243
00:22:57,800 --> 00:22:58,440
What did I tell you?

244
00:22:58,840 --> 00:23:00,840
Wow, you should see your face.

245
00:23:00,840 --> 00:23:02,120
Here you go, as ordered, sir.

246
00:23:15,960 --> 00:23:18,120
Is this the client
you’re designing a mascot for?

247
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:19,960
They didn’t give me much to work with.

248
00:23:20,560 --> 00:23:21,160
Just this photo.

249
00:23:22,320 --> 00:23:22,920
Isn’t that good?

250
00:23:23,520 --> 00:23:25,800
You can sell any idea.

251
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:28,720
Who told you that?

252
00:23:29,320 --> 00:23:31,720
Any job with no clear brief is the hardest.

253
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:33,560
Have you been to this place?

254
00:23:36,520 --> 00:23:37,520
No, I haven’t.

255
00:23:38,600 --> 00:23:40,320
I think I’ll have to make time to go there.

256
00:23:41,520 --> 00:23:45,800
I can’t really picture it from just one photo.

257
00:23:45,880 --> 00:23:46,600
How are you getting there?

258
00:23:46,960 --> 00:23:48,120
Do you know the way?

259
00:23:51,120 --> 00:23:53,920
I guess I’ll take a van.

260
00:23:56,960 --> 00:23:57,960
Sounds like a hassle.

261
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:02,320
What else can I do? I don’t have a car.

262
00:24:04,280 --> 00:24:05,160
What about my car?

263
00:24:06,920 --> 00:24:07,440
What?

264
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:09,480
Are you offering to drive me?

265
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:14,240
We’ve never taken a trip
out of town together.

266
00:24:51,720 --> 00:24:52,200
Moth.

267
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:53,720
Pose for the photos.

268
00:24:56,440 --> 00:24:57,200
Wanna get on that?

269
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:50,480
Here.

270
00:26:24,840 --> 00:26:25,920
Let’s go to this café after.

271
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:27,880
Tons of good reviews.

272
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:29,960
Oh, let’s not.

273
00:26:30,600 --> 00:26:31,760
Those are all paid reviews.

274
00:26:31,760 --> 00:26:33,200
I doubt the actual place
is as nice as the pictures.

275
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:34,560
Don’t go there.

276
00:26:35,720 --> 00:26:37,200
Nice or not, I can decide for myself.

277
00:26:37,280 --> 00:26:39,640
You have to see it for yourself to tell.

278
00:26:40,520 --> 00:26:41,320
No.

279
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:43,960
It’s too far, and it’s not on our way.

280
00:26:44,480 --> 00:26:45,480
Yes, it is.

281
00:26:45,680 --> 00:26:46,160
Look.

282
00:26:50,840 --> 00:26:51,560
What?

283
00:26:52,280 --> 00:26:53,680
What’s stopping you from going?

284
00:26:54,840 --> 00:26:55,880
Is your ex-lover there?

285
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:57,200
No. There’s nothing there.

286
00:26:57,760 --> 00:26:59,240
If you want to go, let’s go.

287
00:27:24,080 --> 00:27:24,960
Just admit it.

288
00:27:25,280 --> 00:27:26,680
Do you have a fling living around here?

289
00:27:27,040 --> 00:27:27,680
No.

290
00:27:28,880 --> 00:27:29,520
You’re overthinking it.

291
00:27:30,480 --> 00:27:31,120
Just order.

292
00:27:34,320 --> 00:27:36,200
Hey, Dean!

293
00:27:38,320 --> 00:27:39,880
Why didn’t you tell me
you were coming home?

294
00:27:58,160 --> 00:28:01,080
You didn’t tell me this is your hometown,

295
00:28:01,400 --> 00:28:02,960
or that this is your big sister’s café.

296
00:28:04,520 --> 00:28:05,440
Why didn’t you say anything?

297
00:28:06,840 --> 00:28:07,880
I didn’t think it was important.

298
00:28:08,440 --> 00:28:09,120
Of course it was.

299
00:28:10,080 --> 00:28:11,960
I told you about my parents.

300
00:28:14,840 --> 00:28:16,360
You think this kind of thing isn’t important?

301
00:28:17,440 --> 00:28:19,400
It is, it is. I’m sorry.

302
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:21,000
Wanna try this?

303
00:28:22,360 --> 00:28:23,280
No, you go ahead.

304
00:28:28,960 --> 00:28:29,760
How is everything?

305
00:28:30,680 --> 00:28:31,920
Is the drink okay?

306
00:28:32,520 --> 00:28:33,240
Yeah, it’s good.

307
00:28:33,680 --> 00:28:35,240
So, what are you guys doing here?

308
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:36,080
Vacation?

309
00:28:36,560 --> 00:28:37,880
I’m here to do some research for work.

310
00:28:38,120 --> 00:28:40,520
I saw your café looked really nice,
so we stopped by.

311
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:44,440
But Dean didn’t tell me anything.

312
00:28:45,040 --> 00:28:45,480
What?

313
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:48,240
Dean didn’t tell you it was my café?

314
00:28:49,480 --> 00:28:52,840
Wow. Were you trying to
keep my café under wraps?

315
00:28:53,080 --> 00:28:54,160
You brat.

316
00:28:54,440 --> 00:28:55,080
Or what?

317
00:28:55,280 --> 00:28:57,160
You didn’t want your boyfriend to meet me?

318
00:29:03,520 --> 00:29:05,560
I’m just a friend. Not his boyfriend.

319
00:29:24,800 --> 00:29:25,360
What?

320
00:29:25,960 --> 00:29:27,240
Is he really not your boyfriend?

321
00:29:27,720 --> 00:29:29,160
- I told you—
- Then what is he?

322
00:29:29,400 --> 00:29:30,520
A friend.

323
00:29:31,240 --> 00:29:32,160
Really.

324
00:29:35,560 --> 00:29:38,840
Be careful with your mixed signals.

325
00:29:39,920 --> 00:29:41,960
Someone else might get to him first.

326
00:29:46,600 --> 00:29:49,160
And I told Mom you’re here.

327
00:29:49,560 --> 00:29:52,160
She told me to drag you home for dinner.

328
00:30:10,160 --> 00:30:11,640
Root for me, baby girl.

329
00:30:19,200 --> 00:30:22,200
Moodeng, have you eaten yet?

330
00:30:22,560 --> 00:30:23,040
Hmm?

331
00:30:23,560 --> 00:30:24,840
Have you had some food?

332
00:30:26,320 --> 00:30:29,480
Wanna go out for a run? Hm?

333
00:30:31,680 --> 00:30:32,560
Am I right?

334
00:30:43,400 --> 00:30:44,640
Gosh, your daddy really sucks.

335
00:30:45,400 --> 00:30:46,360
What should we do?

336
00:30:47,440 --> 00:30:48,560
Should we just go home?

337
00:30:48,840 --> 00:30:49,360
Excuse me.

338
00:30:49,720 --> 00:30:51,040
Are you Mr. Monsieur?

339
00:30:51,160 --> 00:30:51,480
Yes.

340
00:30:51,960 --> 00:30:52,320
Oops.

341
00:30:54,880 --> 00:30:57,200
Holy shit.

342
00:30:59,160 --> 00:31:00,280
It’s nice to finally meet you.

343
00:31:02,240 --> 00:31:02,800
You too.

344
00:31:11,520 --> 00:31:12,080
Ten.

345
00:31:15,960 --> 00:31:16,880
You’re here too?

346
00:31:26,120 --> 00:31:26,680
Hello.

347
00:31:28,120 --> 00:31:31,480
Well, I…

348
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:40,480
A friend of a friend of a friend
who knows me invited me.

349
00:31:40,880 --> 00:31:43,000
I didn’t know I’d run into you here, Dr. Pun.

350
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:44,120
What a coincidence.

351
00:31:44,560 --> 00:31:47,840
I thought you were
someone from the chat room.

352
00:31:51,760 --> 00:31:53,480
Excuse me. I need a refill.

353
00:31:54,600 --> 00:31:55,280
Sure.

354
00:32:02,520 --> 00:32:04,400
Everyone recognizes me, girl,

355
00:32:04,920 --> 00:32:06,720
except the one person
I want to recognize me.

356
00:32:16,120 --> 00:32:18,520
All right, Good Boi Friendly members,

357
00:32:18,520 --> 00:32:20,960
let’s gather around and have a chat.

358
00:32:21,240 --> 00:32:22,240
Please.

359
00:32:22,600 --> 00:32:23,320
Hey there.

360
00:32:24,120 --> 00:32:25,320
Come on in and have a seat.

361
00:32:25,480 --> 00:32:26,960
Wow, he seems to enjoy eating.

362
00:32:27,040 --> 00:32:28,240
- He likes it?
- Yeah.

363
00:32:29,040 --> 00:32:29,920
I knew it.

364
00:32:37,520 --> 00:32:38,480
Alright.

365
00:32:38,560 --> 00:32:42,720
So we finally get to meet after
hearing each other’s voices for so long.

366
00:32:42,800 --> 00:32:44,840
My username is Uncle Peanut Brittle.

367
00:32:46,720 --> 00:32:47,760
Next.

368
00:32:47,760 --> 00:32:49,920
My username is Truffle Pizza.

369
00:32:49,920 --> 00:32:51,000
Oh, he’s Mr. Truffle Pizza.

370
00:32:52,600 --> 00:32:54,440
My username is Mr. Hong.

371
00:32:54,480 --> 00:32:55,840
Hi, Mr. Hong.

372
00:32:56,280 --> 00:32:58,080
I’m Feeding Bowl.

373
00:32:58,240 --> 00:33:00,120
I’m Blossom.

374
00:33:00,160 --> 00:33:02,160
Ms. Blossom, it’s very nice to meet you.

375
00:33:02,240 --> 00:33:03,040
Your turn.

376
00:33:07,760 --> 00:33:08,400
I’m…

377
00:33:13,560 --> 00:33:14,600
I’m not a member of your group.

378
00:33:16,960 --> 00:33:18,880
Wait, aren’t you Mr. Monsieur?

379
00:33:23,920 --> 00:33:27,320
No, I’m Ten, not Monsieur.

380
00:33:27,680 --> 00:33:31,360
But when I called you Monsieur, you nodded.

381
00:33:32,760 --> 00:33:35,760
And your voice
sounds just like Mr. Monsieur’s.

382
00:33:35,760 --> 00:33:36,680
Exactly.

383
00:33:36,680 --> 00:33:39,520
No, no, no. It’s not like that.

384
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:42,600
I thought you called me “mister.”

385
00:33:43,080 --> 00:33:45,240
Like, “Bonjour, Monsieur.”

386
00:33:45,560 --> 00:33:46,280
Something like that.

387
00:33:46,280 --> 00:33:48,280
Come on. Where are we, Paris?

388
00:34:01,720 --> 00:34:03,760
I think everyone’s misunderstanding.

389
00:34:05,960 --> 00:34:09,239
He’s… Mr. Ten.

390
00:34:10,760 --> 00:34:12,600
I know him in real life.

391
00:34:14,360 --> 00:34:16,239
There’s no way he’s Mr. Monsieur.

392
00:34:18,199 --> 00:34:18,840
Mr. Ten, it is.

393
00:34:19,600 --> 00:34:20,760
Nice to meet you, Mr. Ten.

394
00:34:23,520 --> 00:34:25,159
Next, please.

395
00:34:25,159 --> 00:34:27,679
My username is Bagel Smoked Salmon.

396
00:34:27,679 --> 00:34:28,840
Mr. Bagel!

397
00:34:28,840 --> 00:34:31,760
Any dramatic stories to tell us today?

398
00:34:42,360 --> 00:34:43,360
Heading home already?

399
00:34:44,639 --> 00:34:45,000
Yes.

400
00:34:45,320 --> 00:34:46,320
Don’t go yet.

401
00:34:46,760 --> 00:34:47,960
Enjoy it with us a little longer.

402
00:34:48,159 --> 00:34:50,760
Besides, it’s been a while since we last met.

403
00:34:51,639 --> 00:34:52,560
I missed...

404
00:34:58,680 --> 00:34:59,160
All right.

405
00:35:01,400 --> 00:35:03,240
Aw, I missed you so much.

406
00:35:03,320 --> 00:35:05,320
Did you miss me, Mademoiselle?

407
00:35:06,200 --> 00:35:08,240
It’s been a minute, my lady.

408
00:35:48,800 --> 00:35:49,680
Come on.

409
00:35:50,080 --> 00:35:51,600
Mom finished setting the table a while ago.

410
00:35:52,160 --> 00:35:52,920
Let’s go, Moth.

411
00:35:58,240 --> 00:36:01,520
Here we go. Freshly cooked fish.

412
00:36:01,760 --> 00:36:03,680
Does it look good?

413
00:36:08,280 --> 00:36:09,600
When are you going to grow up?

414
00:36:11,040 --> 00:36:13,720
You didn’t even call to say
you were coming home.

415
00:36:14,800 --> 00:36:17,600
You made your mom scramble
to get everything ready.

416
00:36:18,920 --> 00:36:21,680
But I didn’t ask her to.

417
00:36:23,840 --> 00:36:25,560
It’s our family tradition.

418
00:36:26,880 --> 00:36:27,880
Dig in.

419
00:36:28,240 --> 00:36:30,760
My mom’s the best cook in the world.

420
00:36:32,320 --> 00:36:33,640
Here, Moth.

421
00:36:33,960 --> 00:36:34,560
Thank you.

422
00:36:34,640 --> 00:36:36,080
I don’t know why you have to complain.

423
00:36:36,160 --> 00:36:38,680
It’s nice that our son
came home to have dinner with us.

424
00:36:38,720 --> 00:36:39,880
Moth, eat all you want.

425
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:43,000
Dean hardly ever brings friends home.

426
00:36:47,360 --> 00:36:47,960
Yes, ma’am.

427
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:54,680
It’s delicious.

428
00:36:56,480 --> 00:36:57,480
Mom, you eat too.

429
00:36:58,000 --> 00:36:58,880
Stop piling food on everyone’s plate.

430
00:37:00,160 --> 00:37:03,920
Moth has to eat and get back to work quickly.

431
00:37:04,160 --> 00:37:05,520
I’m not in that much of a hurry.

432
00:37:06,560 --> 00:37:08,640
I haven’t had food this good in a long time.

433
00:37:09,760 --> 00:37:13,280
But you said you’d come check the location
and get back to work.

434
00:37:14,240 --> 00:37:17,080
I’m in a rush, just not as much as you are.

435
00:37:17,720 --> 00:37:19,440
Your mom’s cooking is so good. Eat.

436
00:37:23,640 --> 00:37:26,520
You know, Dean was very quiet as a kid.

437
00:37:26,840 --> 00:37:28,680
His teacher told me he didn’t talk much.

438
00:37:29,040 --> 00:37:30,680
All he did was read.

439
00:37:30,840 --> 00:37:34,680
But now, watching his videos,
he seems like a completely different person.

440
00:37:34,760 --> 00:37:36,000
He’s so talkative.

441
00:37:37,640 --> 00:37:38,560
That’s interesting.

442
00:37:39,240 --> 00:37:40,480
I never knew this side of him.

443
00:37:42,680 --> 00:37:43,440
Mom.

444
00:37:44,240 --> 00:37:45,840
Don’t show him my old photos.

445
00:37:45,920 --> 00:37:46,760
And why would you tell him that?

446
00:37:48,120 --> 00:37:48,920
Moth, look at this.

447
00:37:49,120 --> 00:37:50,720
Dean in glasses.

448
00:37:50,760 --> 00:37:52,000
Look at that round face.

449
00:37:53,120 --> 00:37:56,720
Dean doesn’t tell me much about his life.

450
00:37:57,440 --> 00:37:59,440
How is he in Bangkok?

451
00:37:59,560 --> 00:38:01,160
Does he have lots of friends?

452
00:38:02,320 --> 00:38:05,640
Well, yes, he does.

453
00:38:07,160 --> 00:38:08,280
A lot, indeed.

454
00:38:09,040 --> 00:38:10,080
That’s great.

455
00:38:10,120 --> 00:38:13,120
Next time, bring your friends home with you.

456
00:38:14,240 --> 00:38:15,080
Come on, Mom.

457
00:38:15,400 --> 00:38:16,360
My friend has to go back now.

458
00:38:17,200 --> 00:38:18,240
He’s got work.

459
00:38:18,520 --> 00:38:20,880
What? You’re not staying the night?

460
00:38:21,960 --> 00:38:23,200
Can you stay one night?

461
00:38:26,120 --> 00:38:27,480
We can’t this time.

462
00:38:28,840 --> 00:38:29,920
Deadline’s pretty tight.

463
00:38:37,960 --> 00:38:39,480
Here, take this with you.

464
00:38:40,800 --> 00:38:42,720
Wow, it’s a lot. I can’t finish all this.

465
00:38:44,040 --> 00:38:45,760
Come here. Give me a hug.

466
00:38:45,880 --> 00:38:47,040
All right.

467
00:38:48,840 --> 00:38:50,280
Drive safe.

468
00:38:50,400 --> 00:38:52,440
Get back to Bangkok safe and sound.

469
00:38:52,720 --> 00:38:54,760
And if you have time, come home for a visit.

470
00:38:54,960 --> 00:38:56,560
If I get the chance, I will.

471
00:38:57,200 --> 00:38:59,200
That’s what you always say.

472
00:38:59,400 --> 00:39:01,720
Get going. Let me know
when you get to Bangkok.

473
00:39:01,840 --> 00:39:02,560
Sure, Mom.

474
00:39:02,720 --> 00:39:03,320
Let me have a kiss.

475
00:39:05,720 --> 00:39:06,360
See you.

476
00:39:09,240 --> 00:39:10,760
Goodbye, ma’am.

477
00:39:11,440 --> 00:39:12,280
Thank you for the food.

478
00:39:14,480 --> 00:39:17,520
I should be thanking you, Moth.

479
00:39:18,360 --> 00:39:19,720
Please take care of Dean.

480
00:39:20,320 --> 00:39:24,000
He lives alone in Bangkok
and never tells us anything.

481
00:39:24,320 --> 00:39:27,600
But knowing he has you with him
puts my mind at ease.

482
00:39:30,320 --> 00:39:30,800
Yes, ma’am.

483
00:39:33,240 --> 00:39:34,120
Let’s go already.

484
00:39:36,280 --> 00:39:36,920
Bye now.

485
00:39:37,760 --> 00:39:38,480
See you, Mom.

486
00:39:41,120 --> 00:39:42,200
Come visit again.

487
00:40:02,680 --> 00:40:04,200
(Mr. Monsieur has joined us.)

488
00:40:04,480 --> 00:40:05,880
(Where did you go today?)

489
00:40:11,720 --> 00:40:12,440
I…

490
00:40:14,160 --> 00:40:15,920
I was sick. That’s why I didn’t show up.

491
00:40:16,560 --> 00:40:17,720
(You really weren’t there?)

492
00:40:17,760 --> 00:40:20,200
(Someone claimed to be Monsieur today.)

493
00:40:20,840 --> 00:40:21,880
I really wasn’t there.

494
00:40:22,440 --> 00:40:24,680
Maybe he misunderstood
and thought you greeted him in French.

495
00:40:24,720 --> 00:40:29,200
(Hold on. You didn’t go, but you sure
sound like you knew what happened.)

496
00:40:30,760 --> 00:40:32,680
Sorry, I’m late.

497
00:40:33,560 --> 00:40:35,240
It’s good you’re here, Mr. Bagel.

498
00:40:35,720 --> 00:40:37,680
What are we talking about today?

499
00:40:38,760 --> 00:40:42,640
Before we start,
have something to tell you guys.

500
00:40:43,520 --> 00:40:47,560
From now on, I won’t have time
to come online and chat with you.

501
00:40:53,040 --> 00:40:58,080
I’ll be very busy with work and personal stuff.

502
00:41:00,360 --> 00:41:05,680
I didn’t tell you all at the event today
because I was afraid you’d be sad.

503
00:41:07,920 --> 00:41:14,200
Even if I’m no longer on this app,
you can still come see me at my clinic.

504
00:41:14,640 --> 00:41:17,040
(Wait! Mr. Bagel, are you a doctor?)

505
00:41:17,800 --> 00:41:21,520
That’s right. My name is Pun,

506
00:41:21,520 --> 00:41:23,000
and I’m a veterinarian.

507
00:41:23,200 --> 00:41:25,200
I run a clinic called Buddy Heal.

508
00:41:26,120 --> 00:41:29,440
If you see me, come say hi.

509
00:41:29,600 --> 00:41:32,680
(What a shame. I won’t get to
hear your voice anymore, Mr. Bagel.)

510
00:41:32,760 --> 00:41:33,280
(Exactly.)

511
00:41:33,720 --> 00:41:35,560
(Hey, we should call him Dr. Pun now.)

512
00:41:37,440 --> 00:41:38,160
Dr. Pun!

513
00:41:40,520 --> 00:41:40,960
Yes?

514
00:41:41,440 --> 00:41:42,560
Wait for me.

515
00:41:43,160 --> 00:41:44,440
I’m coming to see you at the clinic.

516
00:41:47,760 --> 00:41:50,960
If you are, you’d better head out now.

517
00:41:52,960 --> 00:41:55,640
We close at nine.

518
00:41:57,640 --> 00:41:58,600
8:30 PM

519
00:41:58,600 --> 00:41:59,440
Shit.

520
00:42:04,640 --> 00:42:06,240
(Hey, do you hear someone running?)

521
00:42:06,240 --> 00:42:07,360
(Mr. Monsieur?)

522
00:42:07,840 --> 00:42:09,640
(Go say goodbye to
Mr. Bagel before he leaves.)

523
00:42:12,800 --> 00:42:15,320
(The roads to Dr. Pun’s clinic
are all red on the map.)

524
00:42:16,240 --> 00:42:18,120
(Whoa. Traffic is horrible today.)

525
00:42:19,880 --> 00:42:21,520
(Will Mr. Monsieur make it in time?)

526
00:42:21,880 --> 00:42:23,000
8:45 PM

527
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:24,320
Mr. Bagel, traffic is completely jammed.

528
00:42:24,760 --> 00:42:25,640
Please wait for me.

529
00:42:25,640 --> 00:42:27,760
8:45 PM

530
00:42:43,240 --> 00:42:44,360
(I’m helping you find a way.)

531
00:42:44,840 --> 00:42:45,680
Damn it, the traffic.

532
00:42:45,680 --> 00:42:47,400
(There’s a small alley behind the market.)

533
00:42:48,040 --> 00:42:52,120
Bro, go behind the market. In there. Go!

534
00:42:53,880 --> 00:42:55,120
8:55 PM

535
00:42:57,240 --> 00:42:58,520
(The road in front of the clinic is jammed.)

536
00:42:58,520 --> 00:42:59,400
(You’d better use the one behind it.)

537
00:42:59,400 --> 00:43:01,880
Bro, this alley. Turn here.

538
00:43:02,880 --> 00:43:04,280
8:58 PM

539
00:43:09,840 --> 00:43:12,360
Bro, stop right here at the minimart.

540
00:43:15,280 --> 00:43:16,800
Here. No change.

541
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:26,600
[OPEN DAILY FROM 9 A.M. TO 9 P.M.]

542
00:43:28,960 --> 00:43:31,960
(Mr. Monsieur,
did you make it before Mr. Bagel left?)

543
00:43:32,920 --> 00:43:35,480
(I don’t think he did.)

544
00:43:47,680 --> 00:43:50,680
Dr. Pun, please come out to see me.

545
00:43:51,040 --> 00:43:51,520
Yes.

546
00:44:12,680 --> 00:44:16,440
Dr. Pun, if I confess something,

547
00:44:17,680 --> 00:44:19,240
please don’t be mad at me.

548
00:44:24,360 --> 00:44:25,200
I’m…

549
00:44:33,080 --> 00:44:34,320
I’m Monsieur.

550
00:44:44,200 --> 00:44:47,840
Ah. I already knew that.

551
00:45:08,600 --> 00:45:12,200
I thought you were
someone from the chat room.

552
00:45:15,040 --> 00:45:17,160
My name is Ten, not Monsieur.

553
00:45:18,800 --> 00:45:21,480
Hello. I’m Long Arm T-Rex.

554
00:45:23,840 --> 00:45:26,840
Is there anything
you want to tell me, Mr. Monsieur?

555
00:45:28,880 --> 00:45:29,920
There isn’t.

556
00:45:34,080 --> 00:45:35,760
[GENTLE FOX]

557
00:45:35,760 --> 00:45:37,320
The day we went to the blind date event,

558
00:45:38,080 --> 00:45:41,800
I already knew you were Long Arm T-Rex.

559
00:45:42,960 --> 00:45:44,400
You knew that day?

560
00:45:44,800 --> 00:45:45,560
No.

561
00:45:46,520 --> 00:45:47,920
I’ve known all along,

562
00:45:48,280 --> 00:45:50,520
and I couldn’t help feeling disappointed.

563
00:45:52,200 --> 00:45:56,920
I thought you were going to tell me
that you were Monsieur.

564
00:45:59,040 --> 00:46:05,360
Dr. Pun, aren’t you mad
that I hid it from you?

565
00:46:07,280 --> 00:46:08,880
And that I…

566
00:46:11,040 --> 00:46:13,320
lied to you so many times?

567
00:46:14,040 --> 00:46:17,560
I kind of understand why you did it.

568
00:46:19,000 --> 00:46:25,600
But at least today, I’m glad
you finally had the courage to come see me.

569
00:46:45,760 --> 00:46:46,600
So…

570
00:46:48,640 --> 00:46:50,600
Now that we’ve revealed our real identities,

571
00:46:53,000 --> 00:46:56,440
how about we start going out?

572
00:47:08,680 --> 00:47:11,480
♪ I want your love, so I gave you mine ♪

573
00:47:11,560 --> 00:47:14,280
♪ The love is clear in every sign ♪

574
00:47:14,280 --> 00:47:16,720
♪ What’s your answer, will you approve? ♪

575
00:47:16,720 --> 00:47:20,160
♪ Will you admit you love me too? ♪

576
00:47:20,200 --> 00:47:22,800
♪ There’s nothing I wouldn’t do ♪

577
00:47:22,800 --> 00:47:25,320
♪ Every bit of my heart belongs to you ♪

578
00:47:25,320 --> 00:47:27,400
♪ Giving you love, hoping you’ll reciprocate ♪

579
00:47:27,640 --> 00:47:31,040
♪ So tell me, are we on the same page? ♪

580
00:47:35,600 --> 00:47:39,320
♪ So tell me, are we on the same page? ♪

581
00:47:46,760 --> 00:47:48,240
Can I crash at your place tonight?

582
00:47:51,880 --> 00:47:53,040
You should go home tonight.

583
00:47:56,760 --> 00:47:57,480
I’m sorry.

584
00:47:58,800 --> 00:47:59,280
Huh?

585
00:48:01,680 --> 00:48:03,280
Did I make you uncomfortable?

586
00:48:04,960 --> 00:48:06,360
Why would I be uncomfortable?

587
00:48:07,400 --> 00:48:10,000
Duen even asked to follow you on Instagram.

588
00:48:10,800 --> 00:48:11,880
You didn’t have to accept her request.

589
00:48:13,120 --> 00:48:14,240
Why would I reject it?

590
00:48:16,120 --> 00:48:18,000
It’s just being friends on IG.

591
00:48:18,520 --> 00:48:19,640
And your sister is pretty lovely.

592
00:48:22,000 --> 00:48:24,600
But you don’t usually
accept just anyone’s requests.

593
00:48:25,240 --> 00:48:27,360
Why can’t I be friends with her?

594
00:48:28,920 --> 00:48:30,240
Your family members are pretty nice.

595
00:48:31,440 --> 00:48:35,360
You’re the only one who seems like
you don’t want to talk to them.

596
00:48:39,480 --> 00:48:44,560
And you’re okay with them
thinking we’re together?

597
00:48:46,640 --> 00:48:47,720
Um…

598
00:48:49,480 --> 00:48:52,560
It doesn’t bother me if they think that.

599
00:48:56,160 --> 00:48:56,720
I’m getting off.

600
00:49:12,920 --> 00:49:16,040
Be careful with your mixed signals.

601
00:49:16,880 --> 00:49:18,840
Someone else might get to him first.

602
00:49:32,600 --> 00:49:33,120
Moth.

603
00:49:52,320 --> 00:49:55,080
Why don’t we try… getting together?

604
00:50:45,360 --> 00:50:46,000
Moth.

605
00:50:49,520 --> 00:50:50,880
You’re still the same.

606
00:50:51,040 --> 00:50:53,520
Do you know a guy named Mes?

607
00:50:53,840 --> 00:50:54,880
So you’ve met him?

608
00:50:55,320 --> 00:50:56,440
Yeah, big time.

609
00:50:56,840 --> 00:50:58,480
You’re still so precise with your colors.

610
00:50:58,560 --> 00:51:00,480
I just painted the way my feelings told me to.

611
00:51:01,000 --> 00:51:02,080
Just like you.

612
00:51:02,520 --> 00:51:04,640
Moth, will you start painting again?

613
00:51:05,160 --> 00:51:07,360
Give me a chance to see your work again.

614
00:51:07,680 --> 00:51:09,400
Why don’t you tell him and get it over with?

615
00:51:09,400 --> 00:51:10,720
Tell him you like him.

616
00:51:10,720 --> 00:51:11,600
Are you drunk?

617
00:51:11,600 --> 00:51:12,280
Drunk?

618
00:51:12,680 --> 00:51:13,480
Are you jealous?
